window.EN1_SENSES=[{"word":"fine","form":"fine","common":"好的；晴朗的","sense":"罚款（名词）","note":"金额 $85,000 与入狱处罚并列，fine 指金钱处罚。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2016-636-fine","year":2016,"source":"2016 英语一 · 阅读 Text 1","sentence":"Under the law, using a fashion model that does not meet a government-defined index of body mass could result in a $85,000 fine and six months in prison.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/fine"},{"word":"game","form":"game","common":"游戏；比赛","sense":"供猎捕的野生动物；猎物","note":"生物学家讨论捕食者捕杀体弱动物，game 是动物群体，不能译成游戏。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2010-86-game","year":2010,"source":"2010 英语一 · 翻译","sentence":"(48) Time was when biologists somewhat overworked the evidence that these creatures preserve the health of game by killing the physically weak, or that they prey only on \"worthless\" species.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/game"},{"word":"book","form":"booking","common":"书；预订","sense":"把损失记入账目","note":"宾语是 losses，银行不卖资产，是为了避免确认账面亏损。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2010-69-book","year":2010,"source":"2010 英语一 · 阅读 Text 4","sentence":"And dead markets partly reflect the paralysis of banks which will not sell assets for fear of booking losses, yet are reluctant to buy all those supposed bargains.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/book"},{"word":"air","form":"air","common":"空气","sense":"神态；气派","note":"no air of ... 描述这位音乐家没有令人生畏的指挥家架子。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2011-101-air","year":2011,"source":"2011 英语一 · 阅读 Text 1","sentence":"Even Tommasini, who had advocated Gilbert's appointment in the Times, calls him \"an unpretentious musician with no air of the formidable conductor about him.\" As a description of the next music director of an orchestra that has hitherto been led by musicians like Gustav Mahler and Pierre Boulez, that seems likely to have struck at least some Times readers as faint praise.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/air"},{"word":"novel","form":"novel","common":"小说","sense":"新颖的；前所未有的","note":"novel 修饰 discovery claims，强调发现的新颖性。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2012-243-novel","year":2012,"source":"2012 英语一 · 阅读 Text 3","sentence":"Sometimes years are required for truly novel discovery claims to be accepted and appreciated.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/novel"},{"word":"sound","form":"sound","common":"声音；听起来","sense":"合理的；站得住脚的","note":"legally sound 评价裁决在法律论证上有充分根据。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2017-827-sound","year":2017,"source":"2017 英语一 · 阅读 Text 4","sentence":"The court's ruling is legally sound in defining a kind of favoritism that is not criminal.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/sound"},{"word":"class","form":"class","common":"班级；课程","sense":"格调；品位","note":"cannot buy class 与奖项的 prestige 呼应，强调金钱买不来格调和声望。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2014-463-class","year":2014,"source":"2014 英语一 · 阅读 Text 3","sentence":"You cannot buy class, as the old saying goes, and these upstart entrepreneurs cannot buy their prizes the prestige of the Nobels.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/class"},{"word":"fashion","form":"fashion","common":"时尚","sense":"制定；塑造","note":"fashion 是动词，宾语为 state policies，即制定州政策。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2013-370-fashion","year":2013,"source":"2013 英语一 · 阅读 Text 4","sentence":"Arizona had attempted to fashion state policies that ran parallel to the existing federal ones.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/fashion"},{"word":"cause","form":"causes","common":"原因；导致","sense":"事业；值得支持的公益目标","note":"donate to good causes 是为公益事业捐助，不是捐给原因。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2016-676-cause","year":2016,"source":"2016 英语一 · 阅读 Text 3","sentence":"Second, customers may be willing to buy a company's products as an indirect way to donate to the good causes it helps.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/cause"},{"word":"score","form":"score","common":"分数；得分","sense":"乐谱","note":"前文谈维瓦尔第《四季》，这里把气候数据融入三百年前的乐谱。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2022-1297-score","year":2022,"source":"2022 英语一 · 阅读 Text 3","sentence":"They reimagined the 300-year-old score by injecting the latest climate prediction data for each season—provided by Monash University's Climate Change Communication Research Hub.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/score"},{"word":"spell","form":"spell","common":"拼写","sense":"一段时间","note":"for a spell 与 leaving no lasting benefits 对照：短暂出名，却没留下长远收益。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2020-1054-spell","year":2020,"source":"2020 英语一 · 阅读 Text 1","sentence":"A badly run \"year of culture\" washes in and washes out of a place like the tide, bringing prominence for a spell but leaving no lasting benefits to the community.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/spell"},{"word":"save","form":"save","common":"拯救；节省","sense":"除……以外","note":"unknown save to specialists：除了专家，几乎无人知晓；此处 save 相当于 except。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2010-13-save","year":2010,"source":"2010 英语一 · 阅读 Text 1","sentence":"Yet only one of his books is now in print, and his vast body of writings on music is unknown save to specialists.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/save"},{"word":"call","form":"calling","common":"打电话；呼叫","sense":"使命感很强的职业；天职","note":"as a calling 表示把新闻工作视为一种有使命感的职业。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2010-7-call","year":2010,"source":"2010 英语一 · 阅读 Text 1","sentence":"These men believed in journalism as a calling, and were proud to be published in the daily press.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/call"},{"word":"cover","form":"covered","common":"覆盖","sense":"报道","note":"critics of major papers 与 events 提示，这里说报纸评论家报道的事件。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2010-5-cover","year":2010,"source":"2010 英语一 · 阅读 Text 1","sentence":"In those far-off days, it was taken for granted that the critics of major papers would write in detail and at length about the events they covered.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/cover"},{"word":"turn","form":"turn","common":"转弯；转动","sense":"世纪交替之际","note":"between the turn of the 20th century and ... 表示二十世纪之交到后来某一时点。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2010-4-turn","year":2010,"source":"2010 英语一 · 阅读 Text 1","sentence":"We are even farther removed from the unfocused newspaper reviews published in England between the turn of the 20th century and the eve of World War II, at a time when newsprint was dirt-cheap and stylish arts criticism was considered an ornament to the publications in which it appeared.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/turn"},{"word":"pool","form":"pooling","common":"水池","sense":"集中；汇集","note":"pooling mutual-fund assets 指把共同基金资产汇集起来。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2010-27-pool","year":2010,"source":"2010 英语一 · 阅读 Text 2","sentence":"Curbs on business-method claims would be a dramatic about-face, because it was the Federal Circuit itself that introduced such patents with its 1998 decision in the so-called State Street Bank case, approving a patent on a way of pooling mutual-fund assets.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/pool"},{"word":"position","form":"positions","common":"位置；职位","sense":"立场","note":"take positions in court cases 指在诉讼中表明立场。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2010-31-position","year":2010,"source":"2010 英语一 · 阅读 Text 2","sentence":"Similarly, some Wall Street investment firms armed themselves with patents for financial products, even as they took positions in court cases opposing the practice.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/position"},{"word":"issue","form":"issued","common":"问题；议题","sense":"发布；颁布","note":"issued an unusual order 的宾语是命令，issued 是发布。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2010-33-issue","year":2010,"source":"2010 英语一 · 阅读 Text 2","sentence":"The Federal Circuit issued an unusual order stating that the case would be heard by all 12 of the court's judges, rather than a typical panel of three, and that one issue it wants to evaluate is whether it should \"reconsider\" its State Street Bank ruling.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/issue"},{"word":"critical","form":"critical","common":"批评的","sense":"达到转折阈值的；关键的","note":"critical mass 指足以引发大范围传播的临界数量，并非一群爱批评的人。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2010-52-critical","year":2010,"source":"2010 英语一 · 阅读 Text 3","sentence":"They found that the principal requirement for what is called \"global cascades\" – the widespread propagation of influence through networks – is the presence not of a few influentials but, rather, of a critical mass of easily influenced people.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/critical"},{"word":"compromise","form":"compromised","common":"妥协；折中","sense":"损害；削弱","note":"独立性 is being compromised，意为独立性正在受到损害。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2010-58-compromise","year":2010,"source":"2010 英语一 · 阅读 Text 4","sentence":"The details may be unknowable, but the independence of standard-setters, essential to the proper functioning of capital markets, is being compromised.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/compromise"},{"word":"share","form":"shares","common":"分享","sense":"股票","note":"bank shares rose 表示银行股价上涨。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2010-62-share","year":2010,"source":"2010 英语一 · 阅读 Text 4","sentence":"Bob Herz, the FASB's chairman, cried out against those who \"question our motives.\" Yet bank shares rose and the changes enhance what one lobbying group politely calls \"the use of judgment by management.\"","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/share"},{"word":"interest","form":"interests","common":"兴趣","sense":"利益集团","note":"special interests 指有特定利益诉求的群体，这些群体反对规则清理。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2010-73-interest","year":2010,"source":"2010 英语一 · 阅读 Text 4","sentence":"The FASB and IASB have been exactly that, cleaning up rules on stock options and pensions, for example, against hostility from special interests.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/interest"},{"word":"account","form":"accounts","common":"账户","sense":"叙述；说法","note":"read these ... accounts 指阅读这些迂回的论述。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2010-83-account","year":2010,"source":"2010 英语一 · 翻译","sentence":"It is painful to read these roundabout accounts today.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/account"},{"word":"plant","form":"Plant","common":"植物；种植","sense":"工厂","note":"a telephone-parts factory 已说明 Hawthorne Plant 是工厂名。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2010-x0-plant","year":2010,"source":"2010 英语一 · 完形","sentence":"In 1924 America's National Research Council sent two engineers to supervise a series of experiments at a telephone-parts factory called the Hawthorne Plant near Chicago.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/plant"},{"word":"stem","form":"stems","common":"植物的茎","sense":"源于；起因于","note":"stem from 后接观察结果，指研究者的论点由此而来。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2010-47-stem","year":2010,"source":"2010 英语一 · 阅读 Text 3","sentence":"The researchers' argument stems from a simple observation about social influence: With the exception of a few celebrities like Oprah Winfrey – whose outsize presence is primarily a function of media, not interpersonal, influence – even the most influential members of a population simply don't interact with that many others.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/stem"},{"word":"post","form":"post","common":"邮寄；邮件","sense":"职位","note":"a CEO post 是首席执行官职位。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2011-118-post","year":2011,"source":"2011 英语一 · 阅读 Text 2","sentence":"In recent weeks the No. 2 executives at Avon and American Express quit with the explanation that they were looking for a CEO post.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/post"},{"word":"sit","form":"sitting","common":"坐","sense":"现任的；在职的","note":"sitting CEOs 指仍在任的首席执行官，与已离职的求职者对照。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2011-126-sit","year":2011,"source":"2011 英语一 · 阅读 Text 2","sentence":"Says Korn/Ferry senior partner Dennis Carey: \"I can't think of a single search I've done where a board has not instructed me to look at sitting CEOs first.\"","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/sit"},{"word":"land","form":"landed","common":"土地；着陆","sense":"成功获得（职位）","note":"land in top positions 说的是离职后找到高层职位。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2011-127-land","year":2011,"source":"2011 英语一 · 阅读 Text 2","sentence":"Those who jumped without a job haven't always landed in top positions quickly.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/land"},{"word":"traffic","form":"traffic","common":"交通；车辆","sense":"网站流量","note":"上下文是自有媒体及网站内容，traffic 指访问量。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2011-143-traffic","year":2011,"source":"2011 英语一 · 阅读 Text 3","sentence":"We define such sold media as owned media whose traffic is so strong that other organizations place their content or e-commerce engines within that environment.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/traffic"},{"word":"voice","form":"voice","common":"声音","sense":"表达；说出","note":"voice their opinions 中 voice 作动词，宾语是意见。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2011-147-voice","year":2011,"source":"2011 英语一 · 阅读 Text 3","sentence":"The same dramatic technological changes that have provided marketers with more (and more diverse) communications choices have also increased the risk that passionate consumers will voice their opinions in quicker, more visible, and much more damaging ways.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/voice"},{"word":"concern","form":"concerned","common":"担心；忧虑","sense":"有关的；涉及的","note":"all companies concerned 指所有相关企业；后置的 concerned 不是说它们很焦虑。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2011-146-concern","year":2011,"source":"2011 英语一 · 阅读 Text 3","sentence":"Besides generating income, the presence of other marketers makes the site seem objective, gives companies opportunities to learn valuable information about the appeal of other companies' marketing, and may help expand user traffic for all companies concerned.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/concern"},{"word":"will","form":"will","common":"将；愿意","sense":"意志；意愿（名词）","note":"desire and will 并列作主语，讨论欲望和意志。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2011-174-will","year":2011,"source":"2011 英语一 · 翻译","sentence":"Since desire and will are damaged by the presence of thoughts that do not accord with desire, Allen concluded: \"We do not attract what we want, but what we are.\" Achievement happens because you as a person embody the external achievement; you don't \"get\" success but become it.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/will"},{"word":"matter","form":"matter","common":"事情；问题","sense":"物质","note":"mind 与 matter 对举，讨论精神与物质的关系。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2011-172-matter","year":2011,"source":"2011 英语一 · 翻译","sentence":"Because most of us believe that mind is separate from matter, we think that thoughts can be hidden and made powerless; this allows us to think one way and act another.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/matter"},{"word":"discipline","form":"disciplines","common":"纪律","sense":"学科","note":"humanities 是人文学科，比较的是不同学科的职业化程度。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2011-x0-discipline","year":2011,"source":"2011 英语一 · 新题型 选段A","sentence":"No disciplines have seized on professionalism with as much enthusiasm as the humanities.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/discipline"},{"word":"school","form":"schools","common":"学校","sense":"学院","note":"大学内部 liberal-arts 与 professional education 在不同学院分别教授。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2011-x13-school","year":2011,"source":"2011 英语一 · 新题型 选段D","sentence":"One reason why it is hard to design and teach such courses is that they cut across the insistence by top American universities that liberal-arts education and professional education should be kept separate, taught in different schools.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/school"},{"word":"body","form":"body","common":"身体","sense":"一批；大量（资料、研究）","note":"a body of research 指一批相关研究成果。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2012-200-body","year":2012,"source":"2012 英语一 · 阅读 Text 1","sentence":"An emerging body of research shows that positive health habits—as well as negative ones—spread through networks of friends via social communication.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/body"},{"word":"subject","form":"subject","common":"学科；主题","sense":"受……支配；取决于","note":"be subject to approval 表示须经批准。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2012-210-subject","year":2012,"source":"2012 英语一 · 阅读 Text 2","sentence":"In 2006, the state went a step further, requiring that any extension of the plant's license be subject to the Vermont legislature's approval.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/subject"},{"word":"credit","form":"credit","common":"信用；学分","sense":"认可；功劳","note":"发现者因发现获得学术上的承认，不是获得贷款或课程学分。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2012-233-credit","year":2012,"source":"2012 英语一 · 阅读 Text 3","sentence":"Once a discovery claim becomes public, the discoverer receives intellectual credit.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/credit"},{"word":"reason","form":"reason","common":"原因","sense":"推理；论证（动词）","note":"We reason together 中 reason 是谓语，指共同推理。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2012-245-reason","year":2012,"source":"2012 英语一 · 阅读 Text 3","sentence":"\"We reason together, challenge, revise, and complete each other's reasoning and each other's conceptions of reason.\"","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/reason"},{"word":"bear","form":"borne out","common":"熊；忍受","sense":"证实；支持","note":"be borne out by the analysis 指得到分析的证实；句中 neither 表示两者均未得到证实。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2012-310-bear","year":2012,"source":"2012 英语一 · 翻译","sentence":"Neither of these patterns is borne out by the analysis, suggesting that the structures of the languages are lineage-specific and not governed by universals.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/bear"},{"word":"justice","form":"justices","common":"正义；公正","sense":"法官（尤指高等法院法官）","note":"Supreme Court justices 指最高法院法官。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2012-x0-justice","year":2012,"source":"2012 英语一 · 完形","sentence":"The ethical judgments of the Supreme Court justices have become an important issue recently.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/justice"},{"word":"bear","form":"bears","common":"熊；忍受","sense":"具有；带有","note":"bear little similarity 表示几乎没有相似之处。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2012-x7-bear","year":2012,"source":"2012 英语一 · 新题型 选段E","sentence":"The challenge the computer mounts to television thus bears little similarity to one format being replaced by another in the manner of record players being replaced by CD players.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/bear"},{"word":"volume","form":"volumes","common":"音量；一卷书","sense":"数量；批量","note":"order in volumes 指大批量订货，会消耗大量自然资源。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2013-320-volume","year":2013,"source":"2013 英语一 · 阅读 Text 1","sentence":"For H&M to offer a $5.95 knit miniskirt in all its 2,300-plus stores around the world, it must rely on low-wage overseas labor, order in volumes that strain natural resources, and use massive amounts of harmful chemicals.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/volume"},{"word":"effect","form":"effected","common":"影响；效果（名词）","sense":"使发生；实现（动词）","note":"change can be effected 指变革得以实现；注意与 affect（影响）区分。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2013-326-effect","year":2013,"source":"2013 英语一 · 阅读 Text 1","sentence":"Though several fast-fashion companies have made efforts to curb their impact on labor and the environment – including H&M, with its green Conscious Collection line – Cline believes lasting change can only be effected by the customer.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/effect"},{"word":"fine","form":"fine-grained","common":"好的；晴朗的","sense":"细密的；精细的","note":"fine-grained information 指细粒度信息；这里选取的是复合形容词中的 fine。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2013-332-fine","year":2013,"source":"2013 英语一 · 阅读 Text 2","sentence":"In the past couple of weeks a quarrel has illustrated the value to advertisers of such fine-grained information: Should advertisers assume that people are happy to be tracked and sent behavioural ads?","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/fine"},{"word":"due","form":"due","common":"由于（due to）","sense":"预定的；预计的","note":"be due to do 是预计将做某事；与 due to + 名词表示原因不同。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2013-335-due","year":2013,"source":"2013 英语一 · 阅读 Text 2","sentence":"Microsoft's Internet Explorer and Apple's Safari both offer DNT; Google's Chrome is due to do so this year.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/due"},{"word":"object","form":"objects","common":"物体；对象","sense":"反对（动词）","note":"object to behavioural ads 指反对行为定向广告，to 后为反对的对象。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2013-344-object","year":2013,"source":"2013 英语一 · 阅读 Text 2","sentence":"Unable to tell whether someone really objects to behavioural ads or whether they are sticking with Microsoft's default, some may ignore a DNT signal and press on anyway.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/object"},{"word":"turn","form":"turns on","common":"转弯；转动","sense":"取决于；关键在于","note":"turn on 后接法律主张，指争议的关键所在，不是打开开关。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2013-377-turn","year":2013,"source":"2013 英语一 · 阅读 Text 4","sentence":"The 8-0 objection to President Obama turns on what Justice Samuel Alito describes in his objection as \"a shocking assertion of federal executive power\".","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/turn"},{"word":"strike","form":"strikes","common":"击打；罢工","sense":"使突然想到；使意识到","note":"it strikes one that ... 表示某人突然意识到某事。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2013-404-strike","year":2013,"source":"2013 英语一 · 翻译","sentence":"There is no doubt that gardens evidence an irrepressible urge to create, express, fashion, and beautify and that self-expression is a basic human urge; (46) yet when one looks at the photographs of the gardens created by the homeless, it strikes one that, for all their diversity of styles, these gardens speak of various other fundamental urges, beyond that of decoration and creative expression.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/strike"},{"word":"letter","form":"letter","common":"信；字母","sense":"字面规定","note":"comply ... to the letter 表示严格按法条的字面规定行事。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2013-378-letter","year":2013,"source":"2013 英语一 · 阅读 Text 4","sentence":"The White House argued that Arizona's laws conflicted with its enforcement priorities, even if state laws complied with federal statutes to the letter.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/letter"},{"word":"ground","form":"grounds","common":"地面","sense":"理由；依据","note":"grounds for complaint 是提出抱怨的理由，常用复数。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2014-436-ground","year":2014,"source":"2014 英语一 · 阅读 Text 2","sentence":"But there are few places where clients have more grounds for complaint than America.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/ground"},{"word":"bar","form":"bar","common":"酒吧；栏杆","sense":"法律职业；律师资格","note":"bar exam 是律师资格考试，前文谈成为律师的路径。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2014-442-bar","year":2014,"source":"2014 英语一 · 阅读 Text 2","sentence":"There is just one path for a lawyer in most American states: a four-year undergraduate degree in some unrelated subject, then a three-year law degree at one of 200 law schools authorized by the American Bar Association and an expensive preparation for the bar exam.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/bar"},{"word":"sit","form":"sit","common":"坐","sense":"参加（考试）","note":"sit for the bar 表示参加律师资格考试。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2014-448-sit","year":2014,"source":"2014 英语一 · 阅读 Text 2","sentence":"Another is to let students sit for the bar after only two years of law school.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/sit"},{"word":"body","form":"bodies","common":"身体","sense":"机构；团体","note":"state-level bodies that govern the profession 指管理该行业的州级机构。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2014-446-body","year":2014,"source":"2014 英语一 · 阅读 Text 2","sentence":"Sensible ideas have been around for a long time, but the state-level bodies that govern the profession have been too conservative to implement them.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/body"},{"word":"string","form":"string","common":"绳；线","sense":"一连串；一系列","note":"a string of awards 指接连出现的一系列奖项。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2014-459-string","year":2014,"source":"2014 英语一 · 阅读 Text 3","sentence":"As a News Feature article in Nature discusses, a string of lucrative awards for researchers have joined the Nobel Prizes in recent years.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/string"},{"word":"exercise","form":"exercise","common":"锻炼；练习","sense":"活动；某种做法","note":"an exercise in self-promotion 把设立奖项评价为自我宣传活动。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2014-464-exercise","year":2014,"source":"2014 英语一 · 阅读 Text 3","sentence":"The new awards are an exercise in self-promotion for those behind them, say scientists.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/exercise"},{"word":"row","form":"row","common":"一排；划船","sense":"争吵；争议","note":"row over who is ignored 指围绕谁被遗漏的争议；此义读 /raʊ/。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2014-473-row","year":2014,"source":"2014 英语一 · 阅读 Text 3","sentence":"But the Nobel Foundation's limit of three recipients per prize, each of whom must still be living, has long been outgrown by the collaborative nature of modern research – as will be demonstrated by the inevitable row over who is ignored when it comes to acknowledging the discovery of the Higgs boson.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/row"},{"word":"address","form":"address","common":"地址","sense":"处理；应对","note":"address the ... crisis 的宾语是危机，指处理危机。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2014-482-address","year":2014,"source":"2014 英语一 · 阅读 Text 4","sentence":"Regrettably, however, the report's failure to address the true nature of the crisis facing liberal education may cause more harm than good.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/address"},{"word":"figure","form":"figures","common":"数字；图形","sense":"人物","note":"prominent figures 与外交、电影、音乐等领域连用，指知名人士。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2014-484-figure","year":2014,"source":"2014 英语一 · 阅读 Text 4","sentence":"Among the commission's 51 members are top-tier-university presidents, scholars, lawyers, judges, and business executives, as well as prominent figures from diplomacy, filmmaking, music and journalism.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/figure"},{"word":"bear","form":"bring their learning to bear on","common":"熊；忍受","sense":"把知识运用于……","note":"bring ... to bear on ... 表示运用知识或影响力来解决问题。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2014-487-bear","year":2014,"source":"2014 英语一 · 阅读 Text 4","sentence":"To encourage innovation and competition, the report calls for increased investment in research, the crafting of coherent curricula that improve students' ability to solve problems and communicate effectively in the 21st century, increased funding for teachers and the encouragement of scholars to bring their learning to bear on the great challenges of the day.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/bear"},{"word":"convention","form":"conventions","common":"会议；大会","sense":"惯例；传统做法","note":"harmony and structure 提示这里是音乐和声与结构上的传统惯例。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2014-504-convention","year":2014,"source":"2014 英语一 · 翻译","sentence":"He freed music from hitherto prevailing conventions of harmony and structure.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/convention"},{"word":"account","form":"By all accounts","common":"账户","sense":"据各方面所说","note":"By all accounts 是综合各种说法，不是按所有账户计算。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2014-508-account","year":2014,"source":"2014 英语一 · 翻译","sentence":"(47) By all accounts he was a freethinking person, and a courageous one, and I find courage an essential quality for the understanding, let alone the performance, of his works.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/account"},{"word":"yield","form":"yield","common":"屈服；让步","sense":"产生；提供","note":"发掘工作 yield useful information，即提供有用信息。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2014-x11-yield","year":2014,"source":"2014 英语一 · 新题型 选段C","sentence":"Typically, they survey and sample (make test excavations on) large areas of terrain to determine where excavation will yield useful information.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/yield"},{"word":"room","form":"room","common":"房间","sense":"余地；空间","note":"allow room for police to ... 指为警方保留一定处置余地。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2015-556-room","year":2015,"source":"2015 英语一 · 阅读 Text 2","sentence":"The court, though, may want to allow room for police to cite situations where they are entitled to more freedom.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/room"},{"word":"swallow","form":"swallow","common":"吞咽","sense":"不加质疑地接受","note":"swallow an argument whole 指全盘接受一种论点。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2015-557-swallow","year":2015,"source":"2015 英语一 · 阅读 Text 2","sentence":"But the justices should not swallow California's argument whole.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/swallow"},{"word":"flag","form":"flagged","common":"旗帜","sense":"标记；提醒注意","note":"稿件被 flagged up，是标出来供进一步审查。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2015-564-flag","year":2015,"source":"2015 英语一 · 阅读 Text 3","sentence":"Manuscripts will be flagged up for additional scrutiny by the journal's internal editors, or by its existing Board of Reviewing Editors or by outside peer reviewers.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/flag"},{"word":"drive","form":"drive","common":"驾驶","sense":"有组织的努力；推动行动","note":"Science's overall drive 指期刊提高研究可重复性的整体行动。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2015-566-drive","year":2015,"source":"2015 英语一 · 阅读 Text 3","sentence":"Asked whether any particular papers had impelled the change, McNutt said: \"The creation of the 'statistics board' was motivated by concerns broadly with the application of statistics and data analysis in scientific research and is part of Science's overall drive to increase reproducibility in the research we publish.\"","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/drive"},{"word":"line","form":"line","common":"线；一行字","sense":"立场；方针","note":"take a tougher line 表示采取更强硬的立场。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2015-573-line","year":2015,"source":"2015 英语一 · 阅读 Text 3","sentence":"Researchers should improve their standards, he wrote in 2012, but journals should also take a tougher line, \"engaging reviewers who are statistically literate and editors who can verify the process\".","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/line"},{"word":"home","form":"home","common":"家；在家","sense":"切实被理解；深入人心","note":"drive a point home 表示把观点讲透，让人充分理解。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2015-578-home","year":2015,"source":"2015 英语一 · 阅读 Text 4","sentence":"Driving her point home, she continued: \"It's increasingly apparent that the absence of purpose, of a moral language within government, media or business could become one of the most dangerous goals for capitalism and freedom.\" This same absence of moral purpose was wounding companies such as News International, she thought, making it more likely that it would lose its way as it had with widespread illegal telephone hacking.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/home"},{"word":"charge","form":"charge","common":"收费；充电","sense":"指控；罪名","note":"guilty 与 innocent 围绕审判展开，the same charge 是同一项指控。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2015-579-charge","year":2015,"source":"2015 英语一 · 阅读 Text 4","sentence":"As the hacking trial concludes – finding guilty one ex-editor of the News of the World, Andy Coulson, for conspiring to hack phones, and finding his predecessor, Rebekah Brooks, innocent of the same charge – the wider issue of dearth of integrity still stands.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/charge"},{"word":"betray","form":"betray","common":"背叛","sense":"流露；显露","note":"betray any common humanity 指流露基本人性；原句否定编辑以此为目的。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2015-589-betray","year":2015,"source":"2015 英语一 · 阅读 Text 4","sentence":"The purpose of editing the News of the World was not to promote reader understanding, to be fair in what was written or to betray any common humanity.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/betray"},{"word":"follow","form":"follow","common":"跟随","sense":"由此得出；必然成立","note":"it doesn't necessarily follow that ... 意为不能因此必然得出……。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2015-604-follow","year":2015,"source":"2015 英语一 · 新题型","sentence":"It doesn't then necessarily follow that one kind of reading is fuller, more advanced or more worthwhile than another.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/follow"},{"word":"rate","form":"rate","common":"比率；速度","sense":"评价；把……列为","note":"Britons rate ... as ... 表示英国人把这些事物列为国家自豪的来源。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2016-646-rate","year":2016,"source":"2016 英语一 · 阅读 Text 2","sentence":"While polls show Britons rate \"the countryside\" alongside the royal family, Shakespeare and the National Health Service (NHS) as what makes them proudest of their country, this has limited political support.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/rate"},{"word":"consider","form":"considered","common":"考虑","sense":"经过深思熟虑的","note":"a more considered approach 指更审慎的办法，considered 在此是形容词。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2016-653-consider","year":2016,"source":"2016 英语一 · 阅读 Text 2","sentence":"Only Ukip, sensing its chance, has sided with those pleading for a more considered approach to using green land.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/consider"},{"word":"bank","form":"banking on","common":"银行；河岸","sense":"依赖；指望","note":"bank on the halo effect 指指望光环效应带来好处。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2016-686-bank","year":2016,"source":"2016 英语一 · 阅读 Text 3","sentence":"Nor does it reveal how much companies are banking on the halo effect, rather than the other possible benefits, when they decide their do-gooding policies.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/bank"},{"word":"article","form":"article","common":"文章；冠词","sense":"一件（物品）","note":"one article of clothing at a time 即每次买一件衣服。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2016-741-article","year":2016,"source":"2016 英语一 · 新题型","sentence":"Buy all your clothes at once with a stylist instead of shopping alone, one article of clothing at a time.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/article"},{"word":"line","form":"lines","common":"线；一行字","sense":"排队的队伍","note":"机场 security lines 指安检队伍。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2017-760-line","year":2017,"source":"2017 英语一 · 阅读 Text 1","sentence":"First two hours, now three hours – this is how far in advance authorities are recommending people show up to catch a domestic flight, at least at some major U.S. airports with increasingly massive security lines.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/line"},{"word":"check","form":"checked-baggage","common":"检查","sense":"托运（行李）","note":"checked-baggage fees 是托运行李费；与 carry-on bags 随身行李对照。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2017-770-check","year":2017,"source":"2017 英语一 · 阅读 Text 1","sentence":"Another factor may be that more people are trying to overpack their carry-on bags to avoid checked-baggage fees, though the airlines strongly dispute this.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/check"},{"word":"round","form":"rounded","common":"圆的","sense":"全面的；周全的","note":"a more rounded assessment 与多项评价指标呼应，意为更全面的评估。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2017-810-round","year":2017,"source":"2017 英语一 · 阅读 Text 3","sentence":"Rather than just focusing on GDP, over 40 different sets of criteria from health, education and civil society engagement have been measured to get a more rounded assessment of how countries are performing.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/round"},{"word":"compact","form":"compact","common":"紧凑的","sense":"协议；约定（名词）","note":"the basic compact underlying representative government 指代议制政府所依赖的基本约定。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2017-829-compact","year":2017,"source":"2017 英语一 · 阅读 Text 4","sentence":"\"The basic compact underlying representative government,\" wrote Chief Justice John Roberts for the court, \"assumes that public officials will hear from their constituents and act on their concerns.\"","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/compact"},{"word":"rest","form":"rests on","common":"休息","sense":"建立在……之上","note":"Good governance rests on ... 表示良好治理以某种认识为基础。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2017-836-rest","year":2017,"source":"2017 英语一 · 阅读 Text 4","sentence":"Good governance rests on an understanding of the inherent worth of each individual.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/rest"},{"word":"letter","form":"letters","common":"信；字母","sense":"文学","note":"man of letters 是文学家，呼应狄更斯的小说成就。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2017-x27-letter","year":2017,"source":"2017 英语一 · 新题型 选段G","sentence":"The popularity of these novels consolidated Dickens as a nationally and internationally celebrated man of letters.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/letter"},{"word":"credit","form":"credit","common":"信用；学分","sense":"税额抵免","note":"earned income tax credit 指面向劳动收入的税收抵免，直接减少应缴税额。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2018-877-credit","year":2018,"source":"2018 英语一 · 阅读 Text 1","sentence":"Taxes on low-wage labor need to be cut, and wage subsidies such as the earned income tax credit should be expanded: This would boost incomes, encourage work, reward companies for job creation, and reduce inequality.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/credit"},{"word":"mean","form":"mean","common":"意思是；刻薄的","sense":"怀有……意图","note":"mean well 表示出于好意，并非表示“含义很好”。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2018-900-mean","year":2018,"source":"2018 英语一 · 阅读 Text 3","sentence":"Any fair-minded assessment of the dangers of the deal between Britain's National Health Service (NHS) and DeepMind must start by acknowledging that both sides mean well.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/mean"},{"word":"rate","form":"rate","common":"比率；速度","sense":"资费；收费标准","note":"per-letter 与 penny 明确按信件收取邮资，rate increase 指邮资上涨。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2018-929-rate","year":2018,"source":"2018 英语一 · 阅读 Text 4","sentence":"Most of the money would come from a penny-per-letter permanent rate increase and from shifting postal retirees into Medicare.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/rate"},{"word":"account","form":"accounts for","common":"账户","sense":"占（比例）","note":"后面紧接 80 percent，account for 在此表示费用占比。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2018-932-account","year":2018,"source":"2018 英语一 · 阅读 Text 4","sentence":"There's no change to collective bargaining at the USPS, a major omission considering that personnel accounts for 80 percent of the agency's costs.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/account"},{"word":"bill","form":"bill","common":"账单","sense":"法案","note":"legislators 正在寻求立法共识，bill 指尚待通过的法案。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2018-936-bill","year":2018,"source":"2018 英语一 · 阅读 Text 4","sentence":"The emerging consensus around the bill is a sign that legislators are getting frightened about a politically embarrassing short-term collapse at the USPS.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/bill"},{"word":"court","form":"Court","common":"法庭；球场","sense":"宫廷","note":"这里列举戏剧演出的提供者，Court 指宫廷。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2018-944-court","year":2018,"source":"2018 英语一 · 翻译","sentence":"Court, school, organizations of amateurs, and the traveling actors were all rivals in supplying a widespread desire for dramatic entertainment; and (47) no boy who went to a grammar school could be ignorant that the drama was a form of literature which gave glory to Greece and Rome and might yet bring honor to England.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/court"},{"word":"company","form":"companies","common":"公司；陪伴","sense":"剧团","note":"professional companies 与 theaters 连用，指职业剧团。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2018-949-company","year":2018,"source":"2018 英语一 · 翻译","sentence":"(48) But the professional companies prospered in their permanent theaters, and university men with literary ambitions were quick to turn to these theaters as offering a means of livelihood.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/company"},{"word":"house","form":"housed","common":"房屋","sense":"容纳；为……提供办公场所","note":"大楼 housed 三个行政部门，house 在此用作动词。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2018-x5-house","year":2018,"source":"2018 英语一 · 新题型 选段C","sentence":"The State, War, and Navy Building, as it was originally known, housed the three Executive Branch Departments most intimately associated with formulating and conducting the nation's foreign policy in the last quarter of the nineteenth century and the first quarter of the twentieth century – the period when the United States emerged as an international power.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/house"},{"word":"command","form":"commands","common":"命令","sense":"占有；享有","note":"commands a unique position 指大楼在历史和建筑遗产中占有独特地位。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2018-x12-command","year":2018,"source":"2018 英语一 · 新题型 选段E","sentence":"The Eisenhower Executive Office Building (EEOB) commands a unique position in both the national history and the architectural heritage of the United States.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/command"},{"word":"save","form":"save for","common":"拯救；节省","sense":"除了","note":"most colleges, save for ... 表示大多数高校，除了后文指出的一些高校。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2019-977-save","year":2019,"source":"2019 英语一 · 阅读 Text 2","sentence":"But now most colleges, save for many selective campuses, allow all undergraduates, and even graduate students, to get their low grades forgiven.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/save"},{"word":"mark","form":"marks","common":"标记；分数","sense":"标志着","note":"This year marks ... 表示这一年正逢某个周年节点。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2019-986-mark","year":2019,"source":"2019 英语一 · 阅读 Text 3","sentence":"This year marks exactly two centuries since the publication of \"Frankenstein; or, The Modern Prometheus,\" by Mary Shelley.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/mark"},{"word":"ship","form":"shipping","common":"船","sense":"运送；发货","note":"shipping a customer's purchase to a state 指向某州寄送网购货物，不限定水运。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2019-1012-ship","year":2019,"source":"2019 英语一 · 阅读 Text 4","sentence":"The cases the court overturned said that if a business was shipping a customer's purchase to a state where the business didn't have a physical presence such as a warehouse or office, the business didn't have to collect sales tax for the state.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/ship"},{"word":"lay","form":"lay","common":"放置；下蛋","sense":"非专业的","note":"lay press 指面向普通公众的媒体，与 medical journals 专业医学期刊对照。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2019-1033-lay","year":2019,"source":"2019 英语一 · 翻译","sentence":"(46) There is a great deal of this kind of nonsense in the medical journals which, when taken up by broadcasters and the lay press, generates both health scares and short-lived dietary enthusiasms.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/lay"},{"word":"account","form":"account","common":"账户","sense":"重要性","note":"one of small account 指不甚重要的论文。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2019-1040-account","year":2019,"source":"2019 英语一 · 翻译","sentence":"This is the famed citation index, that is to say the number of times a paper has been quoted elsewhere in the scientific literature, the assumption being that an important paper will be cited more often than one of small account.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/account"},{"word":"code","form":"code","common":"代码；密码","sense":"行为准则","note":"code for the ethical use of AI 指人工智能伦理使用准则。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2019-999-code","year":2019,"source":"2019 英语一 · 阅读 Text 3","sentence":"Whenever decisions are based on masses of data, \"you quickly get into a lot of ethical questions,\" notes Tan Kiat How, chief executive of a Singapore-based agency that is helping the government develop a voluntary code for the ethical use of AI.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/code"},{"word":"cover","form":"cover","common":"覆盖；报道","sense":"足以支付；抵偿","note":"cover the costs 表示用费用抵偿文章准备成本。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2020-1074-cover","year":2020,"source":"2020 英语一 · 阅读 Text 2","sentence":"Publishers have responded to the demand that they make their product free to readers by charging their writers fees to cover the costs of preparing an article.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/cover"},{"word":"pool","form":"pool","common":"水池","sense":"可供选用的人才储备","note":"pool of qualified women 指具备资格的女性人才群体。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2020-1095-pool","year":2020,"source":"2020 英语一 · 阅读 Text 3","sentence":"Writing in The New Republic, Alice Lee notes that increasing the number of opportunities for board membership without increasing the pool of qualified women to serve on such boards has led to a \"golden skirt\" phenomenon, where the same elite women scoop up multiple seats on a variety of boards.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/pool"},{"word":"gross","form":"gross","common":"粗俗的；令人恶心的","sense":"总的；未扣除成本的","note":"gross revenue 是总收入，与扣除成本后的利润不同。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2020-1098-gross","year":2020,"source":"2020 英语一 · 阅读 Text 4","sentence":"Digital services include everything from providing a platform for selling goods and services online to targeting advertising based on user data, and the tax applies to gross revenue from such services.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/gross"},{"word":"register","form":"registered","common":"登记；注册","sense":"被注意到；被感知","note":"眼睛扫视图像，重要细节 registered 指进入视觉认知。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2020-1125-register","year":2020,"source":"2020 英语一 · 新题型","sentence":"These pauses typically occur at about three per second, and the eyes then jump to another spot, until several important points in the image are registered like a series of snapshots.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/register"},{"word":"brand","form":"branded","common":"品牌","sense":"给……扣上名号；污名化","note":"be branded as heresy 指某种理论被斥为异端。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2020-1136-brand","year":2020,"source":"2020 英语一 · 翻译","sentence":"Offering up such a theory during a time of high tension between scientific and religious minds was branded as heresy and any such heretics that continued to spread these lies were to be punished by imprisonment or even death.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/brand"},{"word":"reason","form":"reason","common":"原因","sense":"理性","note":"philosophy founded in reason 指建立在理性基础上的哲学。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2020-1138-reason","year":2020,"source":"2020 英语一 · 翻译","sentence":"It was with these great revelations that a new kind of philosophy founded in reason was born.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/reason"},{"word":"bear","form":"borne","common":"熊；忍受","sense":"承担（费用）","note":"cost ... should be borne by ... 表示费用应由谁承担。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2021-1149-bear","year":2021,"source":"2021 英语一 · 阅读 Text 1","sentence":"Successive governments have permitted such increases on the grounds that the cost of investing in and running the rail network should be borne by those who use it, rather than the general taxpayer.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/bear"},{"word":"case","form":"case","common":"情况；案例","sense":"论据；理由","note":"a strong case that ... 表示支持某一主张的有力理由。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2021-1155-case","year":2021,"source":"2021 英语一 · 阅读 Text 1","sentence":"However, there is a strong case that those who have been worst affected by industrial action should receive compensation for the disruption they have suffered.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/case"},{"word":"industry","form":"industrial action","common":"工业；行业","sense":"劳工行动（如罢工）","note":"industrial action 是劳动关系用语；这里指前文铁路罢工。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2021-1155-industry","year":2021,"source":"2021 英语一 · 阅读 Text 1","sentence":"However, there is a strong case that those who have been worst affected by industrial action should receive compensation for the disruption they have suffered.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/industry"},{"word":"become","form":"becoming","common":"变成","sense":"得体的；好看的","note":"becoming 修饰 look，评价笑容是否体面，不是“正在变成”。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2021-1195-become","year":2021,"source":"2021 英语一 · 阅读 Text 3","sentence":"A toothy grin (especially when there were gaps or blackened gnashers) lacked class: drunks, tramps, and music hall performers might gurn and grin with a smile as wide as Lewis Carroll's gum-exposing Cheshire Cat, but it was not a becoming look for properly bred persons.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/becoming"},{"word":"cap","form":"caps","common":"帽子","sense":"上限","note":"data caps 指数据流量上限。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2021-1205-cap","year":2021,"source":"2021 英语一 · 阅读 Text 4","sentence":"Yet the FCC also ended the investigations of broadband providers that imposed data caps on their rivals' streaming services but not their own.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/cap"},{"word":"bar","form":"bar","common":"酒吧；栏杆","sense":"禁止；阻止","note":"bar ... from doing 表示禁止某人或机构做某事。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2021-1211-bar","year":2021,"source":"2021 英语一 · 阅读 Text 4","sentence":"It needs to give the commission explicit authority once and for all to bar broadband providers from meddling in the traffic on their network and to create clear rules protecting openness and innovation online.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/bar"},{"word":"mark","form":"marked","common":"标记；分数","sense":"显著的；明显的","note":"marked changes 指大学治理安排的明显变化。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2021-1245-mark","year":2021,"source":"2021 英语一 · 翻译","sentence":"In the 1960s and 1970s, European universities saw marked changes in their governance arrangements, with empowerment of junior faculty and to some degree of students as well.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/mark"},{"word":"still","form":"stills","common":"仍然；静止的","sense":"（电影）剧照；静帧","note":"animation stills from Disney films 是动画电影中的静帧图像。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2022-1251-still","year":2022,"source":"2022 英语一 · 阅读 Text 1","sentence":"The variety of plastic objects at risk is dizzying: early radios, avant-garde sculptures, celluloid animation stills from Disney films, the first artificial heart.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/still"},{"word":"bed","form":"beds","common":"床","sense":"花坛","note":"beds of roses 与艺术品中的花朵造型对应，bed 指花坛。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2022-1257-bed","year":2022,"source":"2022 英语一 · 阅读 Text 1","sentence":"Those pieces included small beds of roses and other items as well as a few dozen \"nature carpets\"—large rectangles decorated with foam pumpkins, cabbages, and watermelons.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/bed"},{"word":"case","form":"cases","common":"情况；案例","sense":"保护罩；展柜","note":"sculptures beneath protective cases 指雕塑放在保护罩或展柜下。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2022-1265-case","year":2022,"source":"2022 英语一 · 阅读 Text 1","sentence":"She is proud that several sculptures have even gone on display again, albeit sometimes beneath protective cases.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/case"},{"word":"crop","form":"crop","common":"庄稼；农作物","sense":"一批（同一时期的人）","note":"the latest crop of students 指最新一批申请入学的学生。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2022-1271-crop","year":2022,"source":"2022 英语一 · 阅读 Text 2","sentence":"As the latest crop of students pen their undergraduate application form and weigh up their options, it may be worth considering just how the point, purpose and value of a degree has changed and what Generation Z need to consider as they start the third stage of their educational journey.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/crop"},{"word":"pen","form":"pen","common":"钢笔","sense":"书写；撰写","note":"students pen their ... form 中 pen 是动词，指填写申请表。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2022-1271-pen","year":2022,"source":"2022 英语一 · 阅读 Text 2","sentence":"As the latest crop of students pen their undergraduate application form and weigh up their options, it may be worth considering just how the point, purpose and value of a degree has changed and what Generation Z need to consider as they start the third stage of their educational journey.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/pen"},{"word":"prompt","form":"prompt","common":"迅速的","sense":"促使；引发","note":"prompt new research 指催生新的研究。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2022-1303-prompt","year":2022,"source":"2022 英语一 · 阅读 Text 3","sentence":"Such an approach can both prompt new research as well as result in powerful art.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/prompt"},{"word":"provision","form":"provisions","common":"供给；供应","sense":"条款；规定","note":"these provisions 承接前文雇佣关系法中的规定。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2022-1316-provision","year":2022,"source":"2022 英语一 · 阅读 Text 4","sentence":"But these provisions create difficulties for businesses when applied to highly paid managers and executives.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/provision"},{"word":"contract","form":"contract out of","common":"合同","sense":"以协议约定不受……约束","note":"contract out of the ... regime 指通过合同排除某种制度的适用。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2022-1331-contract","year":2022,"source":"2022 英语一 · 阅读 Text 4","sentence":"In New Zealand, a 2016 private members' Bill tried to permit firms and high-income employees to contract out of the unjustified dismissal regime.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/contract"},{"word":"line","form":"bottom line","common":"线；一行字","sense":"盈利；经营成果","note":"此处比较机构盈利与动物生存状况谁更重要；不是“最低道德底线”。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2022-1339-line","year":2022,"source":"2022 英语一 · 新题型","sentence":"They are profitable institutions whose bottom line is much more important than the condition of the animals.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/line"},{"word":"camp","form":"camp","common":"营地；露营","sense":"阵营","note":"in the same camp as ... 指在动物园问题上属于同一立场阵营。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2022-1354-camp","year":2022,"source":"2022 英语一 · 新题型","sentence":"As a fellow environmentalist, animal-protection advocate and longtime vegetarian, I could properly be in the same camp as Emma Marris on the issue of zoos.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/camp"},{"word":"intelligence","form":"intelligence","common":"智力；智能","sense":"情报","note":"intelligence officers 与 spies 并列，指情报人员。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2022-1374-intelligence","year":2022,"source":"2022 英语一 · 翻译","sentence":"(49) There may have been many spies and intelligence officers during the Napoleonic Wars, but it is usually extremely difficult to find the material they actually provided or worked on.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/intelligence"},{"word":"volume","form":"volumes","common":"音量；书卷","sense":"充分表明；很能说明问题","note":"speak volumes about 是固定表达，说明某事极能反映其背后情况。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2022-1378-volume","year":2022,"source":"2022 英语一 · 翻译","sentence":"(50) Just as the code breaking has its wider relevance in the struggle for Spain, so his attempts to make his way up the promotion ladder speak volumes about British society.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/volume"},{"word":"carry","form":"carry","common":"搬；携带","sense":"持有（保险）","note":"carry insurance 是投保并持有有效保险，承接出租房屋的法规要求。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2023-1410-carry","year":2023,"source":"2023 英语一 · 阅读 Text 2","sentence":"The bill requires every rental host to register with the state, mandates they carry insurance, and opens the potential for local taxes on top of a new state levy.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/carry"},{"word":"title","form":"titles","common":"标题；头衔","sense":"书；出版物","note":"PRH titles 指这家出版社出版的书籍。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2023-1418-title","year":2023,"source":"2023 英语一 · 阅读 Text 3","sentence":"We are not boycotting PRH titles but we are doing our utmost to ensure that availability for customers remains good despite the lower overall levels of stock.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/title"},{"word":"advance","form":"advances","common":"前进；进步","sense":"预付稿酬","note":"出版商合并减少竞价，lower advances 指作者拿到的预付稿酬更低。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2023-1424-advance","year":2023,"source":"2023 英语一 · 阅读 Text 3","sentence":"It comes at a time when authors are already worried about the consequences of the proposed merger between PRH and another big publisher, Simon & Schuster—the reduction in the number of unaligned UK publishers is likely to lead to fewer bidding wars, lower advances, and more conformity in terms of what is published.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/advance"},{"word":"issue","form":"issue","common":"问题；议题","sense":"（期刊的）一期","note":"article in an issue 指某一期期刊中的文章。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2023-1438-issue","year":2023,"source":"2023 英语一 · 阅读 Text 4","sentence":"These journals can act as milk cows where every single article in an issue may cite a specific paper or a series of papers.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/issue"},{"word":"oblige","form":"oblige","common":"迫使；使负有义务","sense":"照办；答应请求","note":"do not oblige 紧接不当引文请求，意为不要按对方要求去做。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2023-1448-oblige","year":2023,"source":"2023 英语一 · 阅读 Text 4","sentence":"And for authors who wish to steer clear of citation cartel activities: when an editor, a reviewer, or a support service asks you to add inappropriate references, do not oblige and do report the request to the journal.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/oblige"},{"word":"flag","form":"Red flags","common":"旗帜","sense":"警示信号","note":"Red flags 指值得警惕的异常迹象，如发表后一年内引文突然激增。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2023-1447-flag","year":2023,"source":"2023 英语一 · 阅读 Text 4","sentence":"Red flags include a large number of citations to an article within the first year.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/flag"},{"word":"starve","form":"starved","common":"挨饿","sense":"严重缺乏","note":"be starved of information 把缺数据比作缺食物，指得不到必需信息。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2023-1463-starve","year":2023,"source":"2023 英语一 · 翻译","sentence":"(49) If customers are not willing to share data, AI will be starved of essential information and will not be able to function effectively or employ machine learning to improve its marketing content and communication.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/starve"},{"word":"spring","form":"springs","common":"春天；弹簧","sense":"泉","note":"hot springs 与 waterfalls 并列，指温泉。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2023-x17-spring","year":2023,"source":"2023 英语一 · 新题型 选段F","sentence":"That's why Hayden's expedition aimed to produce a fuller understanding of the Yellowstone River region, from its hot springs and waterfalls to its variety of flora and fauna.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/spring"},{"word":"sail","form":"sailed","common":"航行；帆","sense":"顺利通过","note":"sail through Congress 指法案轻松获得国会通过。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2023-x19-sail","year":2023,"source":"2023 英语一 · 新题型 选段G","sentence":"The bill proved largely popular and sailed through Congress with large majorities in favor.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/sail"},{"word":"credit","form":"credit","common":"信用；学分","sense":"功劳","note":"most of the credit goes to ... 表示大部分功劳归于某人。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2024-1478-credit","year":2024,"source":"2024 英语一 · 阅读 Text 1","sentence":"According to Sichel, although the falling price of nails was driven partly by cheaper iron and cheaper energy, most of the credit goes to nail manufacturers who simply found more efficient ways to turn steel into nails.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/credit"},{"word":"mirror","form":"mirror","common":"镜子","sense":"反映；仿效","note":"这里用不同年级儿童的交往，模拟狩猎采集社会中混龄玩耍的模式。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2024-1493-mirror","year":2024,"source":"2024 英语一 · 阅读 Text 2","sentence":"Another measure could be encouraging friendships between children in different school years to mirror the unsupervised mixed-age playgroups in hunter-gatherer communities.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/mirror"},{"word":"prompt","form":"prompt","common":"迅速的；促使","sense":"提示词","note":"在图像生成工具中，prompt 指引导生成内容的文字输入。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2024-1512-prompt","year":2024,"source":"2024 英语一 · 阅读 Text 3","sentence":"According to the website Lexica, which tracks over 10 million Stable Diffusion images and prompts, Rutkowski's name has been used as a prompt around 93,000 times.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/prompt"},{"word":"forge","form":"forge","common":"伪造","sense":"建立；促成","note":"forge partnerships 指建立合作关系，与伪造没有关系。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2024-1523-forge","year":2024,"source":"2024 英语一 · 阅读 Text 3","sentence":"One suggestion is that AI models could be trained on images in the public domain, and AI companies could forge partnerships with museums and artists, Ortiz says.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/forge"},{"word":"interest","form":"interests","common":"兴趣","sense":"有共同商业利益的群体","note":"commercial interests 与建筑商、采矿经营者并列，指商业利益群体。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2024-1530-interest","year":2024,"source":"2024 英语一 · 阅读 Text 4","sentence":"This narrowing of the regulatory scope was a victory for builders, mining operators and other commercial interests often at odds with environmental rules.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/interest"},{"word":"tell","form":"telling","common":"告诉；讲述","sense":"说明问题的；有说服力的","note":"one telling example 是一个能清楚说明上下游利益冲突的例子。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2024-1539-tell","year":2024,"source":"2024 英语一 · 阅读 Text 4","sentence":"Pennsylvania farmers, to use one telling example, aren't thinking about next year's blue crab harvest in Maryland when they decide whether to spread animal waste on their fields, yet the runoff into nearby creeks can have enormous impact downstream.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/tell"},{"word":"stake","form":"stakes","common":"桩；打赌的赌注","sense":"利害关系；重大后果","note":"see ... the enormous stakes involved 指认识到湿地保护牵涉的重大利害。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2024-1540-stake","year":2024,"source":"2024 英语一 · 阅读 Text 4","sentence":"And so we would call on state lawmakers from Richmond to Albany to consider reviewing their own wetlands protections and see for themselves the enormous stakes involved.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/stake"},{"word":"sanction","form":"sanctioned","common":"制裁","sense":"正式认可；批准","note":"这里要求确认博物馆藏品取得方式合法，因此是认可这一面，而非惩罚这一面。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2024-1556-sanction","year":2024,"source":"2024 英语一 · 新题型","sentence":"Having said that, I do feel that whatever artifacts find their way to public museums should, in fact, be sanctioned as having been obtained on loan, legally purchased, or obtained by treaty.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/sanction"},{"word":"signature","form":"signature","common":"签名","sense":"独有特征；识别特征","note":"odor signature 指每种植物特有的气味特征。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2024-1578-signature","year":2024,"source":"2024 英语一 · 翻译","sentence":"(49) The volatile chemicals produced by plants can be carried a long way, and they are very characteristic: Each plant or tree has its own particular odor signature.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/signature"},{"word":"commission","form":"commissioned","common":"委员会；佣金","sense":"委托开展","note":"RSC commissioned the study 指皇家莎士比亚剧团委托开展研究。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2025-1589-commission","year":2025,"source":"2025 英语一 · 阅读 Text 1","sentence":"\"The research shows that the way actors work makes a big difference to the way children use language and also how they think about themselves,\" Jacqui O'Hanlon of the Royal Shakespeare Company (RSC), which commissioned the study, said.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/commission"},{"word":"draw","form":"drew on","common":"画；拉","sense":"利用；运用","note":"draw on a wider vocabulary 指运用更丰富的词汇。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2025-1593-draw","year":2025,"source":"2025 英语一 · 阅读 Text 1","sentence":"The peer-reviewed results showed that the target group of pupils drew on a wider vocabulary, used words \"classed as more sophisticated or rarer\", and wrote at greater length.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/draw"},{"word":"scale","form":"scale back","common":"规模；秤","sense":"缩减","note":"scale back research 指减少研究活动的规模。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2025-1601-scale","year":2025,"source":"2025 英语一 · 阅读 Text 2","sentence":"I was shocked to learn recently that some scientists want to scale back their research in an effort to decrease carbon emissions.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/scale"},{"word":"power","form":"power","common":"力量；权力","sense":"为……提供动力或能源","note":"power our intelligence 中 power 是动词，讨论科研和计算所需能源。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2025-1615-power","year":2025,"source":"2025 英语一 · 阅读 Text 2","sentence":"Every day, scientists, technologists and engineers are discovering new ways to exploit renewable energy sources and develop techniques not just to use power more intelligently but to power our intelligence.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/power"},{"word":"rip","form":"rip","common":"撕裂","sense":"提取；复制（音视频数据）","note":"盗版者从合法视频平台提取影视内容，再放到非法平台。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2025-1620-rip","year":2025,"source":"2025 英语一 · 阅读 Text 3","sentence":"But the age of streaming has been a boon for some unintended winners: pirates that use software to rip a film or television show in seconds from legitimate online video platforms and host the titles on their own, illegitimate services, which rake in about $2 billion annually from ads and subscriptions.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/rip"},{"word":"host","form":"host","common":"主人；主持人","sense":"存放并提供（网络内容）","note":"host the titles on ... services 指在平台存放并提供这些影视作品。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2025-1620-host","year":2025,"source":"2025 英语一 · 阅读 Text 3","sentence":"But the age of streaming has been a boon for some unintended winners: pirates that use software to rip a film or television show in seconds from legitimate online video platforms and host the titles on their own, illegitimate services, which rake in about $2 billion annually from ads and subscriptions.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/host"},{"word":"shoulder","form":"shouldered","common":"肩膀","sense":"承担（责任）","note":"shoulder responsibility 指担起责任。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2025-1637-shoulder","year":2025,"source":"2025 英语一 · 阅读 Text 4","sentence":"Libraries and archives have traditionally shouldered the responsibility of organization, preservation, and access to information.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/shoulder"},{"word":"trade","form":"trade","common":"贸易；交易","sense":"职业；手艺","note":"ply their trade 指从事本职工作，此处指研究者开展研究。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2025-1650-trade","year":2025,"source":"2025 英语一 · 阅读 Text 4","sentence":"While future researchers may find the digital realm a challenging place to ply their trade, they won't find it an impossible one.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/trade"},{"word":"pool","form":"pool","common":"水池","sense":"汇集；共用","note":"pool resources 表示集中资源来开展合作研究。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2025-1672-pool","year":2025,"source":"2025 英语一 · 翻译","sentence":"(50) They pool resources, collaborate, think outside the box, and find solutions and ways around obstacles to explore science for the sake of science without the traditional boundaries of working inside a formal setting.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/pool"},{"word":"frame","form":"frames","common":"框架；相框","sense":"（影像的）帧","note":"20 frames a second 是每秒二十帧，是相机拍摄速度。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2025-x7-frame","year":2025,"source":"2025 英语一 · 新题型 选段B","sentence":"A typical digital SLR camera shoots 20 frames a second.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/frame"},{"word":"account","form":"accounts","common":"账户","sense":"记载；叙述","note":"written accounts 指书面历史记载。","kind":"典型僻义","id":"2026-1680-account","year":2026,"source":"2026 英语一 · 阅读 Text 1","sentence":"\"We usually only get the human's side of history through written accounts, but of course written history does not always record exactly how something happened.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/account"},{"word":"credit","form":"credits","common":"信用；学分","sense":"税额抵免","note":"tax credits 表示按条件抵扣应纳税额，不能简单等同贷款。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2026-1697-credit","year":2026,"source":"2026 英语一 · 阅读 Text 2","sentence":"Georgia offers up to 30% in transferable tax credits on film and TV production costs, plus an additional 10% increase on the base tax credit if the project includes a Georgia promotional logo.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/credit"},{"word":"draw","form":"draws on","common":"画；拉","sense":"借助；利用","note":"研究者利用书信、日记、小说与访问笔记作为材料。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2026-1711-draw","year":2026,"source":"2026 英语一 · 阅读 Text 3","sentence":"She draws on letters, diaries and fiction, and a 1939 field notebook of verbatim audience research by Winifred Gill.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/draw"},{"word":"bear","form":"bore","common":"熊；忍受","sense":"带有；留有","note":"树干年轮 bore fire scars，意为保留了火灾留下的伤痕；bore 是 bear 的过去式。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2026-1729-bear","year":2026,"source":"2026 英语一 · 阅读 Text 4","sentence":"Some of the trees he analyzed bore more than 20 fire scars among their rings.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/bear"},{"word":"prescribe","form":"prescribed","common":"开处方","sense":"按计划规定；预先安排","note":"prescribed burns 是有计划实施的控制燃烧，目的在于降低后来野火的强度。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2026-1743-prescribe","year":2026,"source":"2026 英语一 · 阅读 Text 4","sentence":"Research shows that these prescribed burns make subsequent wildfires less severe, even if later fires happen under the most dangerous weather conditions.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/prescribe"},{"word":"advance","form":"advanced","common":"前进；进步","sense":"提出（观点、主张）","note":"educators advanced the idea 表示教育者提出这一教学理念。","kind":"词性转换","id":"2026-1760-advance","year":2026,"source":"2026 英语一 · 翻译","sentence":"(48) Educators advanced the idea of having students complete detailed laboratory exercises in high schools in the belief that such work was beneficial primarily as a way to enhance logical reasoning and observational skills.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/advance"},{"word":"command","form":"command","common":"命令","sense":"吸引；赢得","note":"command public attention 指引起公众关注。","kind":"语境引申","id":"2026-1763-command","year":2026,"source":"2026 英语一 · 翻译","sentence":"(49) It wasn't until the phrase \"scientific literacy\" came along in the 1940s that science had the formidable slogan it needed to command public attention and make improving science education an important national goal.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/command"},{"word":"fine","form":"fine tunes","common":"好的；晴朗的","sense":"微调；精细改善","note":"fine-tune 在这里表示细致改善我们的社会理解能力；原卷写作 fine tunes。","kind":"固定搭配","id":"2026-x14-fine","year":2026,"source":"2026 英语一 · 新题型 选段C","sentence":"Standing in the shoes of others fine tunes our social understanding, useful as we struggle to understand friends, neighbours, customers and co-workers.","dictionary":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/fine"}];
